    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d852">

                <pb facs="0792" n="780" xml:id="pg780"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890E.01/9–1644: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Diplomatic Agent and Consul General at Beirut</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Wadsworth</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Beirut</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-16T19:00:00+02:00">September 16,
                            1944—7 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 16—2:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>191. Legtel 190, September 15, 6 p.m. Foreign Minister informed me that at
                    meeting of Lebanese Cabinet last evening decision was taken to refuse to enter
                    into any treaty negotiations with the French. He understood that Syrian Cabinet
                    was to meet today to take similar decision.</p>
                <p>Spears has just sent me word that Lebanese decision has been formally
                    communicated to him.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Caserta.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wadsworth</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
